      "group": "pinmame.input.switch",
      "reason": "Projected onto the div_ramp Primitive (the ramp-lift flap object the retained script rotates in the same handler): SolRampUp/SolRampDown set Controller.Switch(54) directly in code (RampaMovil.Collidable / div_ramp.ObjRotY are toggled together in the same Sub), matching the manual's own finding that the physical sensor is the B-12576 Ramp Lifting Mechanism's own microswitch (part 5647-12001-00, identical to the part this manual prints for switch 54) rather than a separate playfield object."
    },
    {
      "address": 55,
      "group": "pinmame.input.switch",
      "reason": "Projected onto the Kicker.Drain object (the retained table's drain/outhole entry kicker): the cvpmBallStack class (bsTrough.InitSw 55,58,57,56) manages switches 55-58 internally with no individually named trigger object per address; Kicker.Drain is the one physically-modeled object at the outhole/drain position."
    },
    {
      "address": 2,
      "group": "pinmame.output.solenoid",
      "reason": "Projected onto the RampaMovil moving-ramp object's centroid: SolRampUp/SolRampDown directly toggle RampaMovil.Collidable and rotate the div_ramp flap in the same handler; there is no separate coil-plunger object modeled."
    },
    {
      "address": 3,
      "group": "pinmame.output.solenoid",
      "reason": "Projected onto the RampaMovil moving-ramp object's centroid; see solenoid 2."
    },
    {
